    {
      "body": "SM120 datapoint for W4A16 experts: with nvidia/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-NVFP4 on an RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell Max-Q (main `237d99b4af`, FlashInfer 0.7.2, `--moe-backend b12x` with the b12x module FlashInfer 0.7.2 installs, against MARLIN, which auto-selection picks today; two boots each, prefix caching off), B12X decodes 11.8% faster at c=1, but mean TTFT at 1K input is 55.4% higher, decode TPOT at c=16 is 4.2% higher and output throughput at c=16 is 5.8% lower. b12x 1.5.1 from the `vllm[b12x]` extra gives a similar picture (one boot), and chat GSM8K with thinking off (n=200) is 0.965 with FlashInfer's copy and 0.945 with 1.5.1, against 0.970 on MARLIN.\n",
